  {
   "body": "> > It would still be nice to link to https://nixos.org/manual/nixos/unstable/#modular-services somewhere.\r\n> \r\n> We do this today! It has been linked at options details' entry:\r\n> \r\n> > **About**: [What are modular services?](https://nixos.org/manual/nixos/stable/#modular-services)\r\n\r\nYeah that's already good. I think it might make sense to have it above rather than 'inside' the search results at some point.\r\n \r\n> > (also shouldn't that be in the nixpkgs manual rather than the nixos-manual? I thought kinda the point of modular services was that they're not NixOS-specific :)\r\n> \r\n> Indeed! This point was raised earlier at [NixOS/nixpkgs#432550 (comment)](https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/issues/432550#issuecomment-4255111511), and I've worked on this a bit at [NixOS/nixpkgs#519015](https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/pull/519015).\r\n\r\n:+1: \r\n\r\n",
